{"id":"t_bar_row","name":"Chest-supported T-bar row","cue":"Chest on the pad; row the handles to your lower ribs.","research":"Chest-supported T-bar row machine (plate loaded): chest on a pad tilted 48 deg, trunk 42 deg from vertical, legs straight to slightly bent against an angled foot plate behind. One rigid U-shaped lever (a hub on each front post on a common axis, both arms swinging together 13.5 deg, radius 1.6 m to the grips) with a yoke between the two neutral grips (palms facing, 0.15 H each side of the midline, beside the pad), so both hands always hold a handle; the plates ride on a horn on each arm. Design values (standard technique, not a measured trial): the arms hang under the shoulders with the shoulder blades spread at the stretch (elbow ~10), and finish with the elbows ~40 deg out of the sagittal plane, behind the trunk, elbow ~110, the grips at the lower ribs beside the pad, shoulder blades squeezed (clavicle pro -16). Both hands are solved to the two grips at every phase. Geometry: design/fix/tb.mjs.","targets":{"tol":10,"tolBy":{"shoulder_flexion":25,"shoulder_plane":40,"shoulder_flare":25},"note":"design values (standard technique), not a measured trial","A":{"trunk_flexion":42,"elbow_flexion":10},"B":{"trunk_flexion":42,"elbow_flexion":110}},"muscles":{"primary":["lat","trap_mid","upper_back"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":110,"el":10,"dAz":62,"dEl":10,"fill":0.58,"note":"Research view az 110 (lifter right and behind). Turned 62 deg toward the back (az 172, el 20): both hands, both grips and both arms read from behind (the far arm is no longer hidden by the trunk), the lats, mid traps and upper back face the camera, and the lever arms and plates stand beside the hips."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"tempo":[1,0.2,2.5,0.5],"root":[0,0.5809,-0.3995],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":38},"lumbar":{"flex":2},"thorax":{"flex":2},"neck":{"flex":-22},"head":{"flex":-12},"thigh_l":{"flex":15,"abd":6},"shank_l":{"flex":10},"foot_l":{"dorsi":0},"hand_